d synchronously before the project release starts, so the earlier entry is already gone even though release failed. The definition search runs again and caches a fresh entry.\",\"basis\":\"page\",\"quote\":\"Clearing stays synchronous. The service now returns a promise and the backend awaits it, so a pending or rejected graph release reaches the caller.\",\"confidence\":75},{\"id\":\"Q7\",\"prediction\":\"Before: the worker reports the release as successful; the failure is swallowed, or surfaces only as an unhandled rejection in the worker. After: the rejection reaches the worker's release handler, so the daemon gets a failed release reply carrying the error.\",\"basis\":\"inference\",\"quote\":\"\",\"confidence\":45}]}"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 6756, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 6756}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "35c90059-55e9-4ccf-bb01-83d4a1d455d9", "uuid": "50f59542-adfa-4858-b70b-2398ec8c9a34", "timestamp": "2026-09-13T06:50:55.344Z", "request_id": "req_011CezzdWgwgTdmjqCATbfPt"}
